.Dd October 31, 2026
.Dt GVPROXY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm gvproxy
.Nd userspace network proxy and virtual gateway for virtual machines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl debug
.Op Fl forward-dest Ar dest
.Op Fl forward-identity Ar key
.Op Fl forward-sock Ar socket
.Op Fl forward-user Ar user
.Op Fl listen Ar endpoint
.Op Fl listen-bess Ar socket
.Op Fl listen-qemu Ar socket
.Op Fl listen-stdio Ar pipe
.Op Fl listen-vfkit Ar socket
.Op Fl listen-vpnkit Ar socket
.Op Fl log-file Ar file
.Op Fl mtu Ar mtu
.Op Fl pid-file Ar file
.Op Fl ssh-port Ar port
.Op Fl version
.Op Fl api-token-file Ar file
.Op Fl notification Ar socket
.Op Fl services Ar endpoint
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon is a userspace network proxy and virtual gateway for virtual
machines, containers, and emulators.
It is written in pure Go and based on the
.Lk https://github.com/google/gvisor gVisor
network stack
.Pq pkg/tcpip .
It serves as a high-performance replacement for
.Xr slirp 1
and VPNKit without requiring root privileges or host TUN/TAP devices.
.Pp
Compared to traditional user-mode SLIRP implementations,
.Nm
provides an embedded, configurable DNS server, an internal DHCP server,
dynamic port forwarding, and an administrative HTTP API.
.Pp
On Linux,
.Nm
can provide network connectivity to guests running under
.Xr qemu-system-x86_64 1 ,
User Mode Linux
.Pq UML ,
and systems utilizing
.Xr vsock 7 .
.Pp
.Nm
supports multiple operational modes and subsystems:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Sy Network Gateway and DHCP :
.Nm
operates a virtual network gateway (typically at IP address
.Li 192.168.127.1 )
that serves as the default gateway for guest operating systems.
An integrated DHCP server automatically configures guest networking
parameters, including IP assignment, MTU, DNS servers, and search
domains.
.It
.Sy DNS Server :
The built-in DNS server resolves queries for guest virtual machines and
can be configured to serve static DNS zones.
Guests can query it by specifying
.Li nameserver 192.168.127.1
in
.Pa /etc/resolv.conf .
.It
.Sy Dynamic Port Forwarding :
Ports can be dynamically exposed and unexposed between the host and the
virtual machine without restarting the daemon.
Forwarding can be managed by issuing HTTP requests to the control API
either from the host via a UNIX domain socket or from the guest VM via
.Li http://192.168.127.1:80 .
.It
.Sy Host Management HTTP API :
When started with
.Fl listen
or
.Fl services ,
.Nm
exposes a RESTful HTTP management interface.
This API provides endpoints for packet statistics
.Pq Pa /stats ,
dynamic port mapping
.Pq Pa /services/forwarder/* ,
and network tunneling into guest IP endpoints.
The
.Fl services
flag exposes this same API but omits the
.Pa /connect
endpoint, which is useful when no guest helper daemon is running.
.It
.Sy API Authentication :
Requests from inside the guest to the virtual gateway API
.Pq Li http://192.168.127.1:80
can be secured with Bearer token authentication.
When enabled via
.Fl api-token-file
or the
.Ev GV_API_TOKEN
environment variable, requests must supply an HTTP
.Li Authorization: Bearer
header with the token.
Tokens must be strings of at least 32 characters (commonly 44-character
base64url strings).
Host-side endpoints rely on file system permissions of the listening
UNIX domain socket and remain unauthenticated.
.It
.Sy Lifecycle Notifications :
When configured with
.Fl notification ,
.Nm
emits JSON messages over a UNIX domain socket.
These events indicate when
.Nm
is ready to accept connections
.Pq Dv ready ,
when guest interfaces attach or detach
.Pq Dv connection_established , Dv connection_closed
along with guest MAC addresses, and hypervisor errors
.Pq Dv hypervisor_error .
.It
.Sy Limitations :
ICMP packets are not forwarded outside the virtual network.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl debug
Enable and print verbose debugging information.
.It Fl forward-dest Ar dest
Forward a UNIX domain socket to the guest virtual machine over SSH.
Specifies the target socket path on the guest.
.It Fl forward-identity Ar key
Path to the SSH private identity key used for SSH socket forwarding.
.It Fl forward-sock Ar socket
Path to the local host UNIX domain socket to be forwarded into the guest
virtual machine over SSH.
.It Fl forward-user Ar user
SSH user account used to log in to the guest for UNIX socket forwarding.
.It Fl listen Ar endpoint
Specify a control endpoint URI for the host HTTP management API.
Can be specified multiple times.
Supported schemes include
.Li unix://
(e.g.,
.Li unix:///tmp/network.sock )
and
.Li vsock://
(e.g.,
.Li vsock://:1024 ) .
.It Fl listen-bess Ar socket
Path to a
.Li unixpacket
socket to be used by BESS-compatible applications, such as User Mode
Linux
.Pq UML .
Format is
.Li unixpacket:///path/to/socket .
.It Fl listen-qemu Ar socket
Endpoint socket used for QEMU virtual network communication.
Supported schemes include
.Li unix://
(e.g.,
.Li unix:///tmp/qemu.sock )
and
.Li tcp://
(e.g.,
.Li tcp://0.0.0.0:1234 ) .
.It Fl listen-stdio Ar pipe
Accept network communication through a standard I/O (stdio) pipe.
.It Fl listen-vfkit Ar socket
Path to a
.Li unixgram
socket for vfkit-compatible applications.
Format is
.Li unixgram:///path/to/socket .
.It Fl listen-vpnkit Ar socket
Path to a VPNKit-compatible socket for Hyperkit.
.It Fl log-file Ar file
Output log messages (via logrus) to the specified file path.
.It Fl mtu Ar mtu
Set the Maximum Transmission Unit (MTU) for the virtual network.
The default value is 1500.
.It Fl pid-file Ar file
Write the process ID (PID) of the daemon to the specified file upon
startup.
.It Fl ssh-port Ar port
Port used to access the guest virtual machine over SSH.
Must be an integer between 1024 and 65535.
The default is 2222.
.It Fl version
Print program version information and exit.
.It Fl api-token-file Ar file
Path to a file containing a Bearer token string to authenticate guest VM
requests to the gateway HTTP API.
Leading and trailing whitespace in the file is automatically trimmed.
.It Fl notification Ar socket
Listening UNIX domain socket URI
.Pq e.g., Li unix:///tmp/notification.sock
to which JSON lifecycle events will be delivered.
.It Fl services Ar endpoint
Expose the HTTP services and statistics API without the
.Pa /connect
endpoint.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss QEMU with a UNIX Domain Socket
Start
.Nm
listening on a control socket and a QEMU UNIX domain socket:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gvproxy -debug \\
    -listen unix:///tmp/network.sock \\
    -listen-qemu unix:///tmp/qemu.sock
.Ed
.Pp
Launch QEMU (version 7.2.0 or newer) using a stream socket:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ qemu-system-x86_64 [options] \\
    -netdev stream,id=vlan,addr.type=unix,addr.path=/tmp/qemu.sock \\
    -device virtio-net-pci,netdev=vlan,mac=5a:94:ef:e4:0c:ee
.Ed
.Ss QEMU with a TCP Socket
Run
.Nm
listening for QEMU on a local TCP port:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gvproxy -debug \\
    -listen unix:///tmp/network.sock \\
    -listen-qemu tcp://0.0.0.0:1234
.Ed
.Pp
Launch QEMU connecting to the TCP socket:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ qemu-system-x86_64 [options] \\
    -netdev socket,id=vlan,connect=127.0.0.1:1234 \\
    -device virtio-net-pci,netdev=vlan,mac=5a:94:ef:e4:0c:ee
.Ed
.Ss User Mode Linux (UML) with BESS Socket Transport
Start
.Nm
with a BESS unixpacket socket:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gvproxy -debug \\
    -listen unix:///tmp/network.sock \\
    -listen-bess unixpacket:///tmp/bess.sock
.Ed
.Pp
Start User Mode Linux attached to the socket:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ linux.uml vec0:transport=bess,dst=/tmp/bess.sock,depth=128,gro=1,\\
mac=5a:94:ef:e4:0c:ee root=/dev/root rootfstype=hostfs \\
init=/bin/bash mem=2G
.Ed
.Pp
Configure network routing inside the UML guest:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# ip addr add 192.168.127.2/24 dev vec0
# ip link set vec0 up
# ip route add default via 192.168.127.254
.Ed
.Ss Running with vsock on Linux
Launch
.Nm
on the host with vsock and control endpoints:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ sudo gvproxy -debug \\
    -listen vsock://:1024 \\
    -listen unix:///tmp/network.sock
.Ed
.Pp
Inside the virtual machine, run the forwarder container:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# docker run -d --name=gvisor-tap-vsock --privileged --net=host -it \\
    quay.io/crcont/gvisor-tap-vsock:latest
# ping -c1 192.168.127.1
# curl http://redhat.com
.Ed
.Ss Dynamic Port Forwarding via the Host API
Expose host port 6443 to guest IP 192.168.127.2 on port 6443:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl --unix-socket /tmp/network.sock \\
    http:/unix/services/forwarder/expose -X POST \\
    -d '{"local":":6443","remote":"192.168.127.2:6443"}'
.Ed
.Pp
List all currently exposed ports:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl --unix-socket /tmp/network.sock \\
    http:/unix/services/forwarder/all
.Ed
.Pp
Unexpose host port 6443:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl --unix-socket /tmp/network.sock \\
    http:/unix/services/forwarder/unexpose -X POST \\
    -d '{"local":":6443"}'
.Ed
.Ss Receiving Lifecycle Notifications
Listen for JSON event notifications on a UNIX domain socket:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ nc -k -U -l /tmp/notification.sock
.Ed
.Pp
Start
.Nm
with notification delivery enabled:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gvproxy --notification unix:///tmp/notification.sock
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr curl 1 ,
.Xr qemu-system-x86_64 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr unix 7 ,
.Xr vsock 7 ,
.Xr ip 8
